---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CategoryHub from '../../components/CategoryHub.astro';
import AffiliateDisclosure from '../../components/AffiliateDisclosure.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Event & auction software for nonprofits"
  description="Givebutter vs OneCause and the real cost of gala and auction software: when free event tools are enough and when dedicated software earns its fee."
  section="events-auctions">
  <div class="wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs crumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Events & auctions' }]} />
    <section class="prose" style="margin-top: 1.2rem;">
      <p class="kicker">Category guide</p>
      <h1>Event &amp; auction software</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Event software is the most seasonal line in the stack: intense for a few
        weeks, quiet the rest of the year. Size the tool to the event, not the
        organization.
      </p>

      <h2>How to choose</h2>
      <p>
        A community gala with a silent auction runs well on
        <a href="/go/givebutter" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener">Givebutter</a>:
        mobile bidding, ticketing, and payments included, at zero platform fee
        with donor tips on. A signature event with a live auctioneer, sponsor
        tables, seating charts, and a six-figure target is where
        <a href="/go/onecause" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener">OneCause</a>
        earns its package price (annual plans from about $2,995 plus a
        percentage of funds raised). The fee is insurance on your biggest
        revenue night, and their demo of the mobile-bidding flow is worth the
        hour even if you're a year away from needing it.
      </p>
      <p>
        The math to run: a base package plus around 5% of funds raised weighs
        differently against a $50k event than a $500k one. And whatever runs the
        night, export every bidder and buyer into your CRM the week after; the
        follow-up gifts live there.
      </p>
    </section>

    <CategoryHub category="events-auctions" />

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Events software stays free until <a href="/stacks/5m-plus/">the $5M+
        stack</a>, where a dedicated platform starts to justify itself.
      </p>
      <AffiliateDisclosure />
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
